================================================================================
WHY AGPL-3.0
================================================================================

Sard bundles eSpeak NG, which is GPL-3.0-or-later (see §2 below). Distributing that
binary means the work it is conveyed with must be under a GPL-compatible licence and
must not add restrictions of its own. AGPL-3.0 satisfies both: GPL-3.0 §13 and
AGPL-3.0 §13 expressly permit the two to be combined.

This is also a deliberate choice, not only a constraint. AGPL-3.0 keeps Sard and every
derivative of it open — a fork cannot be closed and sold on — while leaving anyone free
to use the program for any purpose, including commercially. That freedom is what makes
it open source; a licence that withheld it would not be.

